WEBVTT

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.760
The paper's blowing off the Rene.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:47.060
I'm done.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.580
Just a question of protecting it from salmon dust.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.120
How could I get along without you, Wayne?

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:54.430
How can I ever repay you?

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.970
Well, darling, remember, Harlow expects me to...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.860
Oh, can't we forget about Harlow?

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.260
He says it's important.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.720
I have to show him some consideration, don't I, darling?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.760
After all, he is my husband.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:33.520
Does your wife drive a yellow convertible?

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.020
Used to be my convertible.

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.740
She's here, right on time.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.080
Quite a stunning woman, too.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:41.830
You're sure you don't want her back?

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:44.350
Her back?

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:45.690
I'd like to have the convertible.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:46.790
It's a good car.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:50.370
That her?

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:51.900
Yes, Dad.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.380
You two stay in the study.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:54.770
Keep your fingers crossed.

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:55.810
I'll yell if I need you.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:13.900
It was sweet of you to invite me.

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.390
What have you been up to these days, Harlow?

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:23.630
Working, Martini.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:24.350
Love one.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.840
I've been reading about you in the newspapers lately.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:28.680
About me?

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.010
About the, uh, Carol and Grant art studio.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.880
One columnist in particular seems to be giving you quite a lot of free publicity.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:40.000
Writes for the Daily Chronicle.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:41.570
That's Wayne Vincent.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.520
Yes, the studio really owes a lot to Mr. Vincent.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.320
And not just from his plugs and his column, either.

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.330
You might call him a silent partner.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.300
Do you employ him?

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.640
In a way, yes.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.130
As you know, art critics don't make much money.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:03:59.960
So on the...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.100
for a small fee. Mr. Vincent helps me select the right paintings for the right prices.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.820
Carolyn, I'll get to the point. No doubt you're wondering why I asked you here.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:10.660
Naturally.

00:04:12.460 --> 00:04:13.260
I want a divorce.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:20.080
Harlow, I seem to recall a certain day, almost two years ago,

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.940
when you and I agreed that our temperaments just wouldn't make for a happy marriage.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.970
At that time, I suggested divorce myself. You were the one who...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
wanted this arrangement for living separately.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.180
Seems simpler that way.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:37.740
Besides, I never dreamed I'd want to marry again.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.240
Sounds like you're in love.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:43.320
Can you think of any reason why I shouldn't be?

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.310
Yes, I can think of one reason.

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:47.440
What's that?

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.300
You're already married.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.480
That's why I'm asking you to divorce me.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.090
But Harlow, I'm quite happy with our present arrangement.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.710
You know, I've been reading the papers, too.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.170
Your company seems to be expanding by the day.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.180
Now, why should I agree to a set alimony

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.600
when under the present arrangement,

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.820
my own income expands with yours?

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.180
We're not living together.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:13.840
Yet I pay the bills as if we were man and wife.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.910
We are a man and wife.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:18.450
Perhaps you're lonely, darling.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:20.780
Perhaps you'd like me to move back with you again.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.090
Perish the thought.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:27.470
The only way you can perish that thought is to pay for it.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.400
I am paying for it.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.130
I'll continue to pay for it on the first of every month.

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.760
Carolyn, when a man pays for his freedom,

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.160
he'd like to enjoy that freedom.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:38.740
But Harlow, the courts don't allow two parties

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.280
to just agree on a divorce.

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.060
It's done all the time.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.480
Well, it won't be done this time.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.280
I have no intention of suing you.

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:52.210
You'd look pretty silly in court, Harlow, darling,

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.450
trying to tell the court you'd like a divorce just

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.870
so you can marry somebody else.

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:59.970
Suppose I offer you the same person

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.920
in the future that you're getting now.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.000
But that doesn't make sense, dear.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:06.260
Why should I even bother with a divorce

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.040
if I can't better my present arrangement?

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:09.740
How much better do you want it?

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:13.630
Same percentage plus 200,000 cash settlement.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.940
200? Where would I get that?

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.480
I'd have to sell half the firm.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.600
Why don't you sell your father's half?

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:21.730
He's getting old.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.300
It's time the old buzzard retired anyhow.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:25.250
Why?

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:29.940
It's the most expensive market.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.320
Tina, you ever threw away, Harlow.

00:06:32.390 --> 00:06:34.070
It just cost you another $100,000.

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.740
Harlow, losing your temper won't help any.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:40.830
Is this the young lady who changed your mind about marriage?

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:42.760
Yes, Louise Nelson.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:45.620
I'm sorry I didn't meet her before I met you.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.040
But you didn't, darling.

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:49.850
She's cute, Harlow.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:51.930
I'm surprised you don't think she's

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.470
worth enough to warrant offering me a reasonable settlement.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:57.200
I did offer you a reasonable settlement.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:06:59.980
Carolyn, if you'll accept his offer, I'll ask you.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.070
I'll add my check to it, $30,000.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:04.110
$30,000.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.610
That's not a settlement, Pop. That's a tip.

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.030
Things could be a lot worse.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:27.480
Suppose you had to live under the same roof with her.

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.020
I might wind up killing her.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:31.650
Don't say that.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.040
Don't even think it.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.860
Well, you can't blame him for thinking it.

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:37.750
Any way you look at it, a woman's a witch.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.760
And no matter how you spell it.

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:49.290
Miss Allen.

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:50.050
Hi, Otto.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:51.990
I forgot my key again this morning.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:52.850
Will you let me in, please?

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.290
Oh, sure thing.

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.630
You don't have to worry about your key

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:58.310
as long as I've got mine.

00:07:58.550 --> 00:07:59.970
I guess in the future, I better work with you.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.170
I've got a chain around my neck.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.790
There you are, Miss Allen.

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:03.430
Thank you.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:13.880
It's me.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.640
What are you doing here this morning?

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:20.580
It's your day off.

00:08:20.780 --> 00:08:22.760
I was anxious to see what you brought back from the auction.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.000
They're on the divan.

00:08:30.700 --> 00:08:31.760
Oh, it's lovely.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:32.820
Who did it?

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.860
Young chap just out of art school.

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.680
Mr. Vincent heard about him on his last trip to San Francisco.

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:40.220
We got it for $75.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.520
Mr. Vincent thinks we can sell it for $300.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.610
Carolyn, it's an Albert Rene.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:48.300
Huh?

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.400
For only $500.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.340
Must be worth $1,000.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.440
Listen to what art critic Wayne Vincent writes about us today.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.160
Your columnist has just learned that the Carolyn Grant

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.980
studio out Beverly Hills way.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.260
will next week show a collection of Albert René originals,

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:06.060
which should create quite a stir among art lovers.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.840
One painting, a seascape of realistic tone and color,

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.280
is rumored to be one of René's best.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:15.270
We shall be eager to study this fine painting,

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:18.910
which René has so aptly called Grey Sea at Dawn.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.900
With a review like that, you should sell it for more than $1,000.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:22.940
$1,600.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:29.750
But it might be Dick.

00:09:31.560 --> 00:09:33.380
I told him he could pick me up any time after 9.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.500
I'm anxious to meet him, Betty.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:39.000
Where is he taking you, the beach?

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.810
Newport. He bought a new boat.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:44.200
And you bought a yachting cab for $1.98.

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:45.660
Does it look so cheap?

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.120
Well, honey, I'm afraid you just wouldn't create any fashion

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:49.800
news on the yacht club veranda.

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.020
Dick's not taking me to any yacht club.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.720
He keeps his boat right where he works at Bailey's Boat Yard.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.360
He says it's not much of a boat.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.030
What difference does it make if it's only a rowboat?

00:09:59.150 --> 00:09:59.890
He's still the man.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.940
in your life, and you should dress for him.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.080
Why don't you run upstairs and see if you can't find something?

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.060
Try that outfit I was supposed to wear

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:08.420
at the Pacific Yacht Club party.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.960
It's more your size than mine anyhow.

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:11.520
Oh, Carolyn, you're an angel.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.000
If Dick shows up while I'm changing,

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:14.140
will you keep him entertained for me?

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.480
I'll try my best.

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.740
Take your time, dear.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:37.400
I'll get it.

00:10:47.150 --> 00:10:47.650
Come in.

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:51.080
Hello.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.150
I'm Dick Sawyer.

00:10:53.530 --> 00:10:55.450
Betty said I could pick her up any time after 9.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:57.240
Come in, make yourself comfortable.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:58.420
She'll be down in a few minutes.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.560
I'm Carolyn Grant.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:00.400
Want your cigar?

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:01.960
Glad to meet you, Mrs. Grant.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:03.830
The name's Carolyn.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:05.530
Can I get you something to drink?

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:07.220
Oh, nothing, thanks.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:11.200
Betty tells me you bought a new boat.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.420
What kind of a yacht is it, sail or power?

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:19.300
Well, in the first place, you can hardly call it a yacht.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.100
The guy I bought it from is a fisherman.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:22.610
It's a 30-footer.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.470
Needs work, but the engine's in good shape.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:26.310
Does it have a cabin?

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:29.970
Sure, a couple of bunks.

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:30.970
head, galley.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:33.310
In fact, as soon as my rent's up, I'll start living aboard.

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:35.890
What does your perspective wife think

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:37.070
about living aboard a boat?

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.060
Betty doesn't go for it at all.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.800
We'll spend a honeymoon cruising around the island,

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:45.320
but after that, we'll just be using the boat on weekends.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.820
Betty wants to find a little house someplace.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.080
So marriage strands the sailor on the beach.

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:54.440
Well, I'm not the first sailor to get himself beached.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.110
Betty's a wonderful girl.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:11:58.820
I'm happy for you both.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.850
Let's talk about the boat some more.

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.000
Is there any chance you might take a lonely girl for a sail someday?

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:08.100
Sure.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.630
Why don't you drive down the harbor with Betty sometime?

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:11.810
With Betty?

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:14.170
I'd feel like an intruder.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.080
There's an old, old saying, you know,

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.980
two's company and three's a crowd.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.740
Maybe when I'm going down to Laguna one day,

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.860
I could stop by Newport for a few minutes

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.800
just to look the boat over.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:27.620
Oh, sure.

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:29.220
Captain Sawyer?

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:35.200
Wow.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:38.710
Hey, the way you're decked out, you

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:41.250
should be going aboard Mr. Van Asterbilt's 90-foot yaw.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:44.010
Where do you see the tub I'm taking you to?

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:47.650
He calls it a tub and names it Betty the Second after me.

00:12:48.520 --> 00:12:50.280
I ought to give you your diamond ring back.

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:51.460
Good.

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.320
I'll turn it in on a new anchor.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:54.720
It is your new anchor.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.380
Looks like you're hooked, Santa.

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:58.210
You bet he is.

00:12:58.940 --> 00:12:59.720
Thanks, Caroline.

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:00.770
Everything.

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:04.520
See you tomorrow.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:10.880
Fun, you two.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:11.530
Bye-bye.

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:33.430
Be thinking about where you'd like to have lunch.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:35.430
Almost any place is fine, dear.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.240
Tell me, what did your attorney have to say?

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:40.180
Nothing we don't know already.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.640
Carolyn's price for divorce is blackmail.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.530
Robbery, call it whatever you like.

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:48.580
It's legal when a woman calls it alimony.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.070
How about you divorcing her?

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:52.700
No grounds.

00:13:53.490 --> 00:13:55.490
The best solution so far has come from Dad.

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:56.530
What was that?

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.570
He's offered to pay Carolyn's price himself.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.790
$300,000.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:04.400
How could he?

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.510
By following Carolyn's suggestion,

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.510
selling his interest in the company.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.020
Harlow, that company's been his whole life.

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:14.990
You couldn't accept a sacrifice like that from him.

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:15.850
I know I couldn't.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:19.580
Ex, honey, I was hoping you'd say that.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:24.680
Something, I don't know what, but something.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:26.860
I'm going to see her attorney this afternoon.

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:52.780
Well, I'll be on my way. The studio's all yours.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:56.440
I left a well-stocked refrigerator and grocery cabinet.

00:14:57.070 --> 00:14:58.690
You won't even have to go out to the market.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:14:59.980
You want me to stay here?

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:00.620
Well, of course.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:02.800
Have you forgotten this is my day to scout paintings

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.240
with Mr. Vincent in the Laguna?

00:15:04.680 --> 00:15:05.500
Oh, no.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:08.010
I thought you were going next week.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:09.870
Must I really stay?

00:15:10.700 --> 00:15:11.880
Well, do you mean you can't?

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.970
Well, I told Dick I'd drive to Newport this afternoon

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:15.870
when I finished work.

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:18.940
Well, I guess I'll just have to stay myself.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:22.800
I was expecting some people in to look at the Rene paintings.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:25.840
I just can't put a clothes sign on the door.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:26.940
Of course not.

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:29.410
If I don't get to that Laguna exhibit, I'll

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:33.520
Oh, Betty, couldn't you possibly postpone your date with Dick?

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.480
I'm sorry for the misunderstanding.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:38.260
But after all, you did lead me to believe

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.540
you could take over for me.

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:41.610
I know. I will.

00:15:42.480 --> 00:15:43.360
I'll make it up to you.

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:44.250
Thanks.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:46.960
Mind if I put in a call to Newport?

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:47.740
Of course not.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:48.460
Don't be silly.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.620
And tell Dick I'm very sorry for the misunderstanding.

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:53.210
Oh, I'm late.

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:55.210
I was supposed to pick up Mr. Vincent at 9.

00:15:55.530 --> 00:15:57.410
If he calls, tell him I'm on the way over.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:58.390
Thanks, Amelia.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.590
It's sure tough, hon, but what can we do about it?

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.140
If you gotta work, you gotta work.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.790
What do you mean, take some other gal out?

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:22.300
Oh, I might take the boat out for a few hours,

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:24.830
maybe fish a little, but if I go, I'll go along.

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:27.360
What's that?

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:31.510
Sure, sure, Ella.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:37.660
Thanks for the use of the phone.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:38.560
Don't mention it.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:52.700
Hi, Mr. Vincent.

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:53.440
Morning, Betty.

00:16:54.680 --> 00:16:56.060
Isn't your boss on the job yet?

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:58.780
Why, she left here at least a half hour ago.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:16:59.700
Left for where?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.760
For your place.

00:17:00.760 --> 00:17:02.100
She thought you'd be waiting for her.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:03.810
Well, it seems to be a bit of a mix-up.

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.230
Do you mind telling me why she thought I'd be waiting for her?

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:07.910
Well, for the lagoon exhibit.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.540
But that's next week.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:11.820
That's what I thought myself.

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:13.960
Oh, I hope you're right.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:15.260
Are you sure?

00:17:15.480 --> 00:17:16.040
Of course.

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:19.340
As a matter of fact, I should be flying to San Francisco.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:22.340
If something unexpected hadn't turned up,

00:17:22.340 --> 00:17:23.560
I'd be on the plane right now.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.930
Must have slipped Carolyn's mind.

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:29.660
Guess she got mixed up on her dates.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:31.430
Oh, I think she'll realize that when

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:32.390
she finds him not there.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:34.190
If she left half an hour ago, she

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.290
should be back in a few minutes.

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.380
Will you wait for her, Mr. Vincent?

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:39.960
She's expecting some people then to see the new paintings.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.200
I'll wait.

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:42.580
Thanks a lot.

00:17:42.980 --> 00:17:50.950
Hi, Mr. Vincent.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:53.210
Just tell Carolyn I went to Newport after all.

00:17:53.350 --> 00:17:54.090
She'll understand.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:10.660
I'll find Mr. Sawyer.

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:12.480
Dick, he's on his boat.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:13.280
Betty the second.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:15.720
Dick, someone to see you.

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:17.020
Thank you.

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:22.510
Hello there.

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:23.870
Hi, Skipper.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.350
Mind if I inspect your ship?

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:26.470
Glad to see you, Mrs. Grant.

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:29.130
The name is Carolyn, unless you're mad at me.

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:29.660
Oh?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.620
Why should I be mad?

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:32.490
Because I made Betty work today.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:34.180
Well, work's work.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.600
I was passing on my way to Laguna and thought

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:37.860
maybe you'd show me your new boat.

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:39.020
Sure thing.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:40.850
You might find it kind of messy.

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:42.030
I wasn't expecting visitors.

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:43.720
All looks very neat to me.

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:44.640
Like me to show you around?

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:45.300
You mind?

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:45.980
Not at all.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:52.480
The engine's a Grayson Marine Master.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.660
I'd much rather have one of those new baby diesels,

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:56.020
but beggars can't be choosers.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:58.000
A lot of special equipment came with it.

00:18:58.460 --> 00:18:59.980
Automatic pilot, ship ashore form.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.040
Even a new pump from the live bait tank.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:04.480
Oh, what are those long poles?

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:05.410
Outriggers.

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:07.440
They keep your lines from fouling when you troll.

00:19:07.860 --> 00:19:08.220
Troll?

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.120
I guess I'm pretty stupid, Dick.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:11.380
I don't know what that means either.

00:19:11.830 --> 00:19:13.930
Well, you run your fish lines out over the end of the poles,

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.730
swing the poles out to each side of the boat,

00:19:15.870 --> 00:19:17.690
and then throttle down to slow speed,

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:19.030
keep chugging along until you catch a fish.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.020
I hear there's a big run of albacore

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:22.100
outside the harbor right now.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.640
I'm going out and see if I can't catch a few.

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:25.900
Oh, I'm sorry that I'm keeping you from fishing.

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:27.070
I'm in no hurry.

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:28.920
Anybody going with you?

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:29.980
Well...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.540
Well, Betty was.

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:33.820
Until I was mean enough to make her work.

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:37.130
Would I be even meaner if I replaced Betty on this fishing

00:19:37.130 --> 00:19:37.510
jaunt?

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:38.830
How long do you expect to be out?

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:40.610
Oh, a few hours, I guess.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:42.080
Mind if I go along?

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.860
Well, not if you don't mind getting salt

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:46.940
spray all over your clothes.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:48.560
There's quite a chop in the channel today.

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:51.420
I don't mind, not if you'll teach me how to catch albacore.

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:52.420
When do we start?

00:19:53.090 --> 00:19:53.890
It's as easy as this.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:37.480
Thanks, Dick.

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:38.730
You're welcome.

00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:48.960
You know what I've been thinking, Dick?

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:50.430
What's that?

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:55.060
That I'm guilty of a complete breach of yachting etiquette.

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:56.960
Why didn't I bring a bottle of champagne?

00:20:58.070 --> 00:20:59.970
It's customary, isn't it, with a new yacht?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.470
Well, uh, for a new yacht, maybe, but for a tub like this,

00:21:03.550 --> 00:21:04.750
you just bring along a can of beer.

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.220
I didn't even bring that.

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:08.780
How are we going to toast the new boat?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:12.400
Well, if you want to toast, there's a bottle of bourbon

00:21:12.400 --> 00:21:13.240
in my first aid locker.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.500
I keep it there in case the snake bites.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:17.060
Help yourself.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:18.400
You'll also find ice and glasses.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:19.680
Just got around the loaf.

00:21:20.810 --> 00:21:21.950
Be right back, Captain.

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:39.510
Find everything you need down there?

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.710
Everything but the ice.

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:42.430
Oh, it's in the locker under the galley sink.

00:21:42.510 --> 00:21:43.070
I'll get it for you.

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:45.290
Oh, is it safe for you to leave without anybody

00:21:45.290 --> 00:21:46.070
steering the boat?

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:47.720
Nobody is steering the boat.

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:48.460
Iron Mike.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:50.200
Now, don't look so puzzled.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:52.000
Iron Mike's an automatic pilot.

00:21:52.160 --> 00:21:53.780
You can hold the course as well as any helmsman.

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:54.840
Amazing.

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:57.940
How far can this mechanical captain take it?

00:21:58.600 --> 00:21:59.980
Well, do we either hit something?

00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.680
How do you like the book so far?

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:05.020
I like everything about it, Dick.

00:22:06.190 --> 00:22:08.070
I especially like Iron Mike.

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:37.590
Hi, Betty.

00:22:37.830 --> 00:22:40.250
I thought I might be able to catch Dick before he went fishing.

00:22:40.670 --> 00:22:41.330
When did he leave?

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:43.860
They left an hour ago, Dick and the lady.

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:47.520
Did they say when they'd be back?

00:22:48.480 --> 00:22:49.740
No, they didn't say.

00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:52.160
Thanks, Virginia.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:12.920
I'll park it, lady.

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:15.360
About how long do you think you'll be?

00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:17.760
Only a couple of minutes. We're picking someone up.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:18.680
Can I just leave it here?

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:19.600
I'll be fine, miss.

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:22.110
I'll bring him right out, Louise.

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:57.700
I've been looking all over town for you.

00:23:59.060 --> 00:23:59.960
How did you happen to look here?

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:04.000
Tired of touring all the bars, we started to phone.

00:24:04.940 --> 00:24:07.730
Louise is outside. You've been pretty worried.

00:24:09.810 --> 00:24:11.250
I've been pretty worried myself.

00:24:12.520 --> 00:24:16.520
Let's be sensible, boy. You can't solve your problem with that stuff.

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:20.990
How can I solve my problem? You tell me.

00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:22.340
Yes, sir. What'll it be?

00:24:22.590 --> 00:24:23.780
Thank you. We're leaving.

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:26.620
Hate to have Louise see you like this.

00:24:27.340 --> 00:24:28.480
Kept up waiting long enough.

00:24:30.090 --> 00:24:33.300
You said it, Dad. I have kept her waiting long enough.

00:24:34.410 --> 00:24:38.180
Oh, let's face it. Carolyn isn't going to give me a divorce. We all know it.

00:24:39.140 --> 00:24:41.760
I ask a girl like Louise to wait forever?

00:24:42.380 --> 00:24:43.340
You know I can't.

00:24:43.460 --> 00:24:48.680
As soon as she gets out of my life, the better. For her, I mean.

00:24:49.700 --> 00:24:51.120
Did you see Carolyn's attorney?

00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:53.940
Why do you think I'm sitting on this bar stool?

00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:55.320
Was Carolyn there, too?

00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:59.970
Town. Maybe it's a good thing she...

00:25:00.030 --> 00:25:03.040
She wasn't there. I kicked her teeth in.

00:25:03.490 --> 00:25:04.710
What did her attorney say?

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:11.440
Same thing. Divorce on Carolyn's terms or no divorce at all.

00:25:12.220 --> 00:25:16.160
First thing in the morning, I'm going to hire private detectives to watch her day and night.

00:25:16.880 --> 00:25:20.530
We'll get something on that woman, even if we have to frame it ourselves.

00:25:22.230 --> 00:25:23.270
Finish your drink and let's go.

00:25:23.490 --> 00:25:26.620
I'm not going. Why not?

00:25:27.410 --> 00:25:29.810
I'm going to sit right here and drink myself blotto.

00:25:30.540 --> 00:25:31.180
Where's your car?

00:25:31.690 --> 00:25:32.430
The parking lot.

00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:34.140
No one will steal it.

00:25:34.220 --> 00:25:34.740
I locked it.

00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:36.500
I'm not afraid of anyone stealing it.

00:25:37.380 --> 00:25:38.860
I'm worried about you driving it.

00:25:39.850 --> 00:25:40.170
Keys.

00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:41.920
Dad, I know what I'm doing.

00:25:43.820 --> 00:25:44.200
Do you?

00:25:53.720 --> 00:25:56.220
Andy, fill it up, will you?

00:26:28.120 --> 00:26:28.880
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

00:26:38.320 --> 00:26:41.940
Too bad we have to say goodnight, but at least we don't have to say goodbye.

00:26:42.690 --> 00:26:43.110
Don't we?

00:26:43.580 --> 00:26:46.100
There's a dinner dance at the Yacht Club next Saturday night.

00:26:46.100 --> 00:26:47.960
It's formal. You'll have to wear a tuxedo.

00:26:48.180 --> 00:26:50.820
But it'll be a grand time dig, just with a tulle.

00:26:51.680 --> 00:26:52.980
You will take me, won't you?

00:26:53.490 --> 00:26:54.090
How can I?

00:26:54.310 --> 00:26:54.910
Why not?

00:26:56.350 --> 00:26:59.660
Well, because, first reason, I think you forgot something.

00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:00.720
You're married.

00:27:01.040 --> 00:27:01.400
Harlow?

00:27:01.900 --> 00:27:03.100
Don't be silly, darling.

00:27:03.240 --> 00:27:04.260
I can forget Harlow.

00:27:04.520 --> 00:27:05.720
But I can't forget Betty.

00:27:05.900 --> 00:27:06.820
That's reason number two.

00:27:07.180 --> 00:27:08.260
Is there a third reason?

00:27:09.310 --> 00:27:10.470
I don't own a tuxedo.

00:27:11.080 --> 00:27:14.740
When a guy like me buys a boat, there just isn't any money left for one of those yacht club waiters.

00:27:14.920 --> 00:27:15.820
I'll buy you one.

00:27:15.900 --> 00:27:17.480
There's a men's tailor right in my court.

00:27:17.960 --> 00:27:18.500
Are you kidding?

00:27:18.890 --> 00:27:20.670
You think I'd let a woman buy me a suit of clothes?

00:27:20.850 --> 00:27:24.110
Why not, if she has the money, and if it pleases her to buy you a present?

00:27:24.170 --> 00:27:26.250
It wouldn't please me, and I don't think it'd please Betty either.

00:27:26.490 --> 00:27:27.710
What does she have to know?

00:27:29.200 --> 00:27:29.880
Callan.

00:27:30.440 --> 00:27:31.400
Let's get something straight.

00:27:32.430 --> 00:27:34.230
I gave a ring to a girl named Betty Allen.

00:27:34.670 --> 00:27:35.790
I gave it to her if it keeps.

00:27:36.560 --> 00:27:38.620
Well, I'm afraid she'll give it right back to you, darling,

00:27:38.780 --> 00:27:41.020
when she finds you invited me on the little rendezvous

00:27:41.020 --> 00:27:41.840
on your boat today.

00:27:42.290 --> 00:27:43.190
Now, wait a minute, Carolyn.

00:27:43.270 --> 00:27:44.190
Let's get something else straight.

00:27:45.140 --> 00:27:46.640
I didn't invite you on that boat today.

00:27:46.890 --> 00:27:47.910
You invited yourself.

00:27:48.840 --> 00:27:50.180
That's not what I'd tell Betty.

00:27:51.740 --> 00:27:51.960
Oh?

00:27:52.120 --> 00:27:54.050
What would you tell her?

00:27:54.410 --> 00:27:56.910
Well, I'm sure I could invent quite a shocking incident

00:27:56.910 --> 00:27:57.910
if I had to, darling.

00:27:58.910 --> 00:27:59.970
You mean you'd tell her about it?

00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:04.540
Well, only if you forced me to, only if we don't have our date.

00:28:06.480 --> 00:28:09.920
I don't seem to get this. Are you trying to blackmail me?

00:28:10.280 --> 00:28:12.140
Oh, that's a nasty word, darling.

00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:15.380
I must ask you to apologize, and then you can kiss me goodnight.

00:28:16.440 --> 00:28:22.080
Oh, Dick, Betty said to give you this whenever you and Mrs. Grant got back.

00:28:30.570 --> 00:28:31.830
She knew I was going fishing.

00:28:32.950 --> 00:28:34.550
She waited till after sundown.

00:28:35.060 --> 00:28:36.700
Maybe she thought you and Mrs. Grant

00:28:36.700 --> 00:28:38.560
were going a little too long for just fishing.

00:28:40.000 --> 00:28:40.920
See you in the morning, Dick.

00:28:44.620 --> 00:28:46.950
Just a ring, no message.

00:28:48.050 --> 00:28:50.950
If you want a woman's opinion, the ring is message enough.

00:28:52.640 --> 00:28:53.780
No, I'm really in a jam.

00:28:55.720 --> 00:28:58.120
But, Carolyn, will you help me straighten this thing out with Betty?

00:28:58.450 --> 00:28:59.570
Of course I will.

00:29:01.560 --> 00:29:03.670
If. If what?

00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:06.300
If you don't forget about our date Saturday night,

00:29:06.820 --> 00:29:08.200
will you pick me up about seven?

00:29:08.820 --> 00:29:09.840
You must be kidding.

00:29:10.220 --> 00:29:12.120
How can I fix things up with Betty if I take you out?

00:29:12.220 --> 00:29:13.260
What's Betty gonna do on Saturday?

00:29:13.690 --> 00:29:16.900
Oh, I'll see that she has to work at the studio all weekend.

00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:18.460
Kiss me goodnight.

00:29:19.900 --> 00:29:24.650
Carolyn, you know, I spent six years in a merchant marine,

00:29:25.560 --> 00:29:27.600
and I ran into an awful lot of no-good women

00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:29.300
in just about every part of the world.

00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:32.300
But I never once ran into one like you.

00:30:30.250 --> 00:30:30.850
Where were you?

00:30:32.410 --> 00:30:34.270
I don't suppose Betty came back here, did she?

00:30:34.450 --> 00:30:35.710
Yes, she was here earlier.

00:30:36.200 --> 00:30:37.200
She seemed quite upset.

00:30:37.300 --> 00:30:38.380
What happened between you two?

00:30:39.160 --> 00:30:40.140
What did she tell you?

00:30:40.420 --> 00:30:42.800
Oh, nothing, but it was obvious that something had happened.

00:30:43.630 --> 00:30:45.670
She dropped by to pick up a few personal things,

00:30:45.870 --> 00:30:49.000
said she wouldn't be back, but she was quitting her job.

00:30:54.760 --> 00:30:57.700
Wayne, if I can reach her, I'd like to talk to her privately.

00:30:58.200 --> 00:30:59.080
Why don't you run along?

00:30:59.200 --> 00:30:59.640
It's late.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:00.800
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:31:01.570 --> 00:31:05.050
She said earlier this morning that there'd been a bit of a mix-up about the art exhibit.

00:31:05.390 --> 00:31:09.000
Did you really drive all the way to Laguna, or where did you go?

00:31:09.940 --> 00:31:13.780
Wayne, I am well over 21, and you don't happen to be my husband.

00:31:14.100 --> 00:31:16.960
I see no reason why you should demand to know where I went.

00:31:18.140 --> 00:31:20.460
Well, I wasn't demanding. I was just wondering.

00:31:21.490 --> 00:31:23.790
And speaking of where I was, where were you?

00:31:23.970 --> 00:31:26.490
I thought you had to fly to San Francisco today for the paper.

00:31:32.460 --> 00:31:34.340
Carolyn, I've got some bad news for us.

00:31:35.030 --> 00:31:37.310
I won't be flying anywhere for the newspaper again.

00:31:38.340 --> 00:31:39.780
They found out about us.

00:31:42.800 --> 00:31:43.960
About us? What do you mean?

00:31:44.350 --> 00:31:47.030
About my using the column to foster a private enterprise.

00:31:47.410 --> 00:31:49.390
Very serious offense in the newspaper business.

00:31:50.670 --> 00:31:52.330
They dismissed me without notice.

00:31:55.350 --> 00:31:57.250
Oh, don't worry about that, dear.

00:31:57.710 --> 00:31:59.970
With your talent, you can easily get a call.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.540
them into some other paper, and then we can just go on as before.

00:32:03.452 --> 00:32:05.292
Why don't you try the Star Dispatch?

00:32:05.532 --> 00:32:06.832
They sell more papers anyhow.

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:08.720
And if they sell more papers?

00:32:09.500 --> 00:32:10.540
We sell more paintings.

00:32:10.620 --> 00:32:11.880
No, you don't understand.

00:32:12.476 --> 00:32:15.056
I won't be able to write a column for any newspaper in the country.

00:32:15.324 --> 00:32:17.204
or any other type of publication for that matter.

00:32:17.820 --> 00:32:19.160
You mean you've been blacklisted?

00:32:19.900 --> 00:32:20.600
I'm afraid so.

00:32:21.756 --> 00:32:22.756
This really is serious.

00:32:23.644 --> 00:32:26.344
Without the help of your column, my sales are bound to drop.

00:32:26.444 --> 00:32:27.624
But I can still help you buy.

00:32:27.996 --> 00:32:29.996
Well, how much buying can I do of myself?

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:32.000
We'll retrench, Carolyn.

00:32:33.356 --> 00:32:35.436
After all, we have one thing to be thankful for.

00:32:36.428 --> 00:32:37.408
We still have each other.

00:32:37.528 --> 00:32:38.848
But you have no job.

00:32:39.180 --> 00:32:41.420
What do you expect me to do, support you from now on?

00:32:41.460 --> 00:32:42.380
No, of course not.

00:32:42.420 --> 00:32:44.260
I can find some other work in another line,

00:32:44.340 --> 00:32:45.540
something not in the art field.

00:32:45.740 --> 00:32:47.980
Well, what else do you know except in the art field?

00:32:48.716 --> 00:32:51.196
Well, good of you to me if you work in some gas station.

00:32:51.564 --> 00:32:54.484
If I need my car washed, I'll stop at the corner.

00:32:55.820 --> 00:32:56.620
Good night, Wayne.

00:33:01.308 --> 00:33:02.508
I don't believe it.

00:33:03.132 --> 00:33:06.452
I lose my job, my career, my future in the art business.

00:33:06.672 --> 00:33:08.752
All for you, and now you throw me out.

00:33:10.556 --> 00:33:12.236
You never cared for me at all, did you?

00:33:12.860 --> 00:33:14.480
Let's not be silly, Wayne.

00:33:15.004 --> 00:33:17.304
If it's love I wanted, I'm still young enough.

00:33:17.384 --> 00:33:19.344
I don't have to settle for a man your age.

00:33:20.796 --> 00:33:22.796
Oh, don't be an old fool!

00:33:38.572 --> 00:33:38.952
Come in.

00:33:43.052 --> 00:33:43.332
Could I?

00:33:43.660 --> 00:33:44.980
Speak to you along, Mrs. Grant.

00:33:45.292 --> 00:33:47.852
Oh, yes, of course. Mr. Vincent was just leaving.

00:33:58.060 --> 00:33:59.740
Will you please be brief? It's late.

00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:03.340
Yes, I know it's late, but I saw your lights,

00:34:03.360 --> 00:34:05.180
and it's most important that I talk to you.

00:34:05.930 --> 00:34:07.830
I'm sure you can guess why I'm here.

00:34:08.150 --> 00:34:11.090
To try and make you see that your present attitude isn't

00:34:11.090 --> 00:34:12.070
helping anyone, Mrs. Grant.

00:34:12.410 --> 00:34:13.360
Not even yourself.

00:34:13.980 --> 00:34:14.960
I'm quite able to.

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:16.500
to look after myself, thank you.

00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:19.620
Must you take care of yourself

00:34:19.620 --> 00:34:21.300
at the expense of three lives?

00:34:22.600 --> 00:34:26.430
Your life, Harlow's, and who's the third person?

00:34:27.480 --> 00:34:28.000
Your own.

00:34:30.476 --> 00:34:30.796
Yep.

00:34:31.340 --> 00:34:31.700
Young.

00:34:32.300 --> 00:34:33.300
Attractive.

00:34:33.388 --> 00:34:34.048
You have talent.

00:34:35.052 --> 00:34:37.472
Harlow's willing to make any kind of a reasonable settlement.

00:34:38.348 --> 00:34:40.188
I'm sure that with all that and your...

00:34:40.188 --> 00:34:43.708
I can take care of my own future in my own way.

00:34:44.108 --> 00:34:44.528
Good night.

00:34:49.740 --> 00:34:51.100
You'll regret this, Mrs. Grant.

00:34:51.500 --> 00:34:53.220
Am I to take that as a threat?

00:34:55.180 --> 00:34:57.180
Take it any way you like.

00:35:14.840 --> 00:35:15.380
Who is it?

00:35:16.070 --> 00:35:17.910
Dick, I've got to talk to you.

00:35:21.030 --> 00:35:22.690
Too late. There's nothing to talk about.

00:35:23.190 --> 00:35:24.270
There's everything to talk about.

00:35:26.940 --> 00:35:28.880
It's no use, Dick. We're finished.

00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:32.330
So you're not even going to give me a chance to explain?

00:35:32.820 --> 00:35:33.820
What's there to explain?

00:35:34.510 --> 00:35:34.790
Everything.

00:35:35.370 --> 00:35:39.450
In the first place, that woman's not worth you and I breaking up over.

00:35:39.760 --> 00:35:40.980
Apparently you thought she was.

00:35:41.140 --> 00:35:42.740
Oh, please, Betty, that's not true.

00:35:43.080 --> 00:35:43.400
Isn't it?

00:35:43.720 --> 00:35:44.940
Listen, honey, I was going to take...

00:35:45.060 --> 00:35:49.120
boat out anyway today. When Carolyn invited herself along, I didn't have any... She didn't

00:35:49.120 --> 00:35:55.230
invite herself. You invited her. Where'd you get that idea? Carolyn, she called me not two minutes

00:35:55.230 --> 00:35:59.920
ago. And told you I invited her on the boat. She also told me you invited her...

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:00.980
for a weekend at the island.

00:36:01.360 --> 00:36:03.540
Of course, invited might not be the right word.

00:36:03.740 --> 00:36:05.380
Honey, that woman's an out-and-out liar.

00:36:05.500 --> 00:36:06.820
I didn't invite her any place.

00:36:07.470 --> 00:36:09.230
Do you expect me to believe that?

00:36:09.450 --> 00:36:10.110
Sure I do.

00:36:10.330 --> 00:36:11.870
Are you going to take her word against the word

00:36:11.870 --> 00:36:12.930
of the man you're engaged to marry?

00:36:13.330 --> 00:36:15.210
The man I was engaged to marry.

00:36:18.400 --> 00:36:20.620
Just leave, Dick, and please don't ever come back.

00:36:21.110 --> 00:36:22.470
Maybe there's still a chance for you

00:36:22.470 --> 00:36:23.870
to lure Carolyn on your boat again.

00:36:24.050 --> 00:36:25.390
And no doubt you can.

00:36:25.900 --> 00:36:26.880
I know Carolyn.

00:36:27.440 --> 00:36:29.780
Yeah, but apparently you don't know me.

00:36:31.240 --> 00:36:34.620
If I ever get her on that boat again, it's going to be for one purpose only.

00:36:34.960 --> 00:36:38.100
To shove her overboard right in the middle of the Pacific Ocean.

00:37:07.100 --> 00:37:08.540
I can sympathize with you, Mr. Grant,

00:37:08.660 --> 00:37:09.800
but I can't give you another drink.

00:37:10.540 --> 00:37:11.720
Look, it's at the 2 in the morning.

00:37:11.820 --> 00:37:12.660
I've got to close up.

00:37:18.190 --> 00:37:18.810
Call a cab, sir?

00:37:21.380 --> 00:37:29.060
We'll try to drive, will you, sir?

00:37:31.690 --> 00:37:32.350
I can't drive.

00:37:33.910 --> 00:37:35.550
Where did I get plastered tonight?

00:37:35.810 --> 00:37:38.550
I can't say as I blame you, Mr. Grant.

00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:41.740
That wife of yours is having the louse you say she is.

00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:43.350
It's enough to make a man want to...

00:37:46.030 --> 00:37:46.970
You're absolutely right.

00:37:47.970 --> 00:37:49.190
With a dull knife.

00:37:53.270 --> 00:37:54.170
Don't do it, Mr. Grant.

00:37:55.150 --> 00:37:57.390
No woman is with a man going to the gas chamber for her.

00:37:59.370 --> 00:37:59.970
Not so sure.

00:38:01.380 --> 00:38:02.920
This one might be worth it.

00:38:04.310 --> 00:38:04.770
Good night, Sam.

00:38:40.680 --> 00:38:41.480
Daddy, is that you?

00:39:06.810 --> 00:39:06.950
Thank you.

00:39:30.410 --> 00:39:32.760
Don't! Oh, don't do it!

00:40:17.760 --> 00:40:18.120
This is great.

00:41:00.480 --> 00:41:00.740
Yes.

00:41:01.120 --> 00:41:01.820
It's an emergency.

00:41:02.780 --> 00:41:16.870
If you want any more pictures, Lieutenant,

00:41:16.990 --> 00:41:18.690
I'll have to go out to the car and get some flash bulbs.

00:41:19.510 --> 00:41:20.430
That's all right. We're covered.

00:41:20.650 --> 00:41:21.350
That'll be it, boys.

00:41:33.360 --> 00:41:34.980
Hello, this is Lieutenant Colton putting me

00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:36.400
through to Captain Horstetter homicide.

00:41:38.360 --> 00:41:39.820
Teddy, here's the score.

00:41:40.750 --> 00:41:44.790
Full name's Carolyn Ellenson Grant, age 29, married.

00:41:45.090 --> 00:41:47.210
But she hadn't been living with her husband for two years.

00:41:47.480 --> 00:41:48.680
They didn't get along together.

00:41:49.670 --> 00:41:50.890
Sure, I'll talk to the husband.

00:41:51.460 --> 00:41:54.520
Name's Harlow Grant, connected with some local chemical

00:41:54.520 --> 00:41:55.060
company.

00:41:56.880 --> 00:41:59.760
I got his home address from the man who found the body, Otto

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.560
She's the janitor here.

00:42:01.780 --> 00:42:03.100
A caretaker, sir.

00:42:03.670 --> 00:42:04.530
Oh, caretaker.

00:42:06.840 --> 00:42:10.140
Any REO also gave me the address of a young woman named Betty Allen.

00:42:10.710 --> 00:42:12.770
Seems she worked for Mrs. Grant in the art business,

00:42:12.950 --> 00:42:13.890
but they had a disagreement.

00:42:14.720 --> 00:42:15.960
Betty Allen quit her job.

00:42:17.740 --> 00:42:18.680
Sure, I'll talk to her.

00:42:18.740 --> 00:42:21.500
I sent Wells to pick them both up, the husband and the Allen girl.

00:42:41.960 --> 00:42:43.180
Well's just coming in, I'll call you back.

00:42:45.710 --> 00:42:48.400
Miss Allen, Miss Grant, this is Lieutenant Colton.

00:42:49.070 --> 00:42:50.970
The sergeant says that she was murdered.

00:42:51.610 --> 00:42:52.710
You don't think it was a burglar.

00:42:52.830 --> 00:42:56.400
A burglar doesn't leave a handbag with $500 in it.

00:42:56.620 --> 00:42:58.480
To say nothing of the jewelry on the dresser upstairs

00:42:58.480 --> 00:42:59.680
and all this art down here.

00:43:00.060 --> 00:43:01.120
Then who do you suspect?

00:43:01.780 --> 00:43:03.320
We were hoping that you could help us.

00:43:04.260 --> 00:43:05.060
I don't think I can.

00:43:06.440 --> 00:43:07.420
What about you, Miss Allen?

00:43:08.230 --> 00:43:09.590
I'm afraid I can't help either.

00:43:12.020 --> 00:43:14.180
When did you last see Carolyn Grant?

00:43:14.980 --> 00:43:16.710
Well, about a week ago.

00:43:16.860 --> 00:43:18.500
She stopped by my house for cocktails.

00:43:20.130 --> 00:43:21.290
And you, Miss Allen?

00:43:22.350 --> 00:43:23.130
Yesterday morning.

00:43:25.620 --> 00:43:29.420
The caretaker says that you came around here and quit your job.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:30.580
Last night.

00:43:31.620 --> 00:43:33.260
I did come here in the early evening,

00:43:33.300 --> 00:43:34.280
but I didn't see Carolyn.

00:43:35.030 --> 00:43:36.950
She'd gone to Lagoon, and she wasn't home yet.

00:43:37.580 --> 00:43:38.400
So I left.

00:43:39.600 --> 00:43:41.700
As I was leaving, I saw out of the caretaker,

00:43:41.780 --> 00:43:42.740
and I told him I was quitting.

00:43:43.360 --> 00:43:44.280
Why were you quitting?

00:43:47.640 --> 00:43:48.260
To get married.

00:43:48.840 --> 00:43:50.640
Are you sure about that, Miss Allen?

00:43:51.370 --> 00:43:52.950
The caretaker said you were upset.

00:43:53.460 --> 00:43:55.440
You and Mrs. Grant didn't quarrel, did you?

00:43:56.250 --> 00:43:58.140
No, of course not.

00:43:58.740 --> 00:43:59.960
We were always the best of you.

00:44:00.520 --> 00:44:02.750
Miss Allen, how long have you been engaged?

00:44:04.550 --> 00:44:07.500
About almost five months now.

00:44:09.900 --> 00:44:10.940
Don't you have an engagement ring?

00:44:12.900 --> 00:44:13.520
I do.

00:44:13.840 --> 00:44:16.270
But it's at the jewelers now.

00:44:16.370 --> 00:44:17.570
I lost a small stone.

00:44:17.810 --> 00:44:19.290
I haven't told Dick about it yet.

00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:27.560
Mr. Grant, her wife died shortly after 3 a.m.

00:44:27.800 --> 00:44:28.560
Her watch stopped.

00:44:28.780 --> 00:44:29.960
It broke when she fell down.

00:44:30.400 --> 00:44:36.550
Well, I thought you... You mean she was killed by a fall?

00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:38.300
She was killed by a gun.

00:44:39.770 --> 00:44:41.550
We're going to have to ask both you and Miss Allen

00:44:41.550 --> 00:44:43.290
to prove where you were at 3 a.m.

00:44:45.010 --> 00:44:48.040
In other words, I have to produce a witness for that hour?

00:44:48.670 --> 00:44:52.280
Exactly. Where were you, Miss Allen?

00:44:53.070 --> 00:44:53.910
At my apartment.

00:44:54.470 --> 00:44:54.870
Alone?

00:44:55.880 --> 00:44:58.240
No. Dick was with me till...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.700
Oh, almost four, and then he drove back to Newport.

00:45:03.230 --> 00:45:04.450
He lives in Newport?

00:45:04.710 --> 00:45:07.330
Yes, he lives on his boat at Bailey's Boat Yard.

00:45:07.790 --> 00:45:09.410
If we should have to talk to him, Miss Allen,

00:45:09.630 --> 00:45:11.470
I promise not to disclose the secret

00:45:11.470 --> 00:45:13.110
of your missing engagement ring.

00:45:13.680 --> 00:45:15.500
So you can entrust us with his full name.

00:45:15.870 --> 00:45:16.290
What is it?

00:45:17.320 --> 00:45:19.290
Dick Sawyer, Richard Sawyer.

00:45:26.040 --> 00:45:26.860
I'm William Vincent.

00:45:27.720 --> 00:45:29.860
I've been a friend of Mrs. Grant's for quite some time.

00:45:31.050 --> 00:45:32.050
This is quite a shock.

00:45:33.090 --> 00:45:35.150
I stopped by to see if she'd have breakfast with me,

00:45:35.210 --> 00:45:36.870
and I saw the police cars outside.

00:45:37.050 --> 00:45:38.470
The caretaker told me what had happened.

00:45:39.000 --> 00:45:40.380
When was the last time you saw Mrs. Grant?

00:45:40.830 --> 00:45:41.430
Last night.

00:45:41.960 --> 00:45:42.240
Where?

00:45:42.590 --> 00:45:43.590
Right here in this room.

00:45:43.980 --> 00:45:44.840
What time, Mr. Vincent?

00:45:45.970 --> 00:45:48.170
Well, it was past 12, because I didn't get home

00:45:48.170 --> 00:45:48.850
until after 1.

00:45:49.250 --> 00:45:52.010
Mrs. Grant seemed nervous, worried, upset about anything.

00:45:52.600 --> 00:45:54.060
Yes, she seemed quite upset.

00:45:54.370 --> 00:45:55.110
Upset about what?

00:45:56.500 --> 00:45:59.280
Well, I don't know, unless, unless?

00:46:00.960 --> 00:46:03.700
A young woman came calling on Mrs. Grant just as I was leaving.

00:46:04.340 --> 00:46:05.140
Do you know who she was?

00:46:07.460 --> 00:46:10.820
Yes, Carolyn pointed her out to me one night in a cafe.

00:46:11.550 --> 00:46:12.890
Her name is Louise Nelson.

00:46:13.970 --> 00:46:17.750
She told me that Harlow Grant and Louise were keeping company.

00:46:20.090 --> 00:46:21.450
Where can we find Louise Nelson?

00:46:25.030 --> 00:46:26.190
914 Longwood Avenue.

00:46:27.860 --> 00:46:28.380
All right, Sergeant.

00:46:57.760 --> 00:46:58.920
Talk to you in a few minutes, Miss Nelson.

00:47:08.670 --> 00:47:09.030
Did you find anything?

00:47:10.760 --> 00:47:11.380
I wish I could.

00:47:12.250 --> 00:47:13.470
Did you find that Nelson girl?

00:47:13.630 --> 00:47:13.870
Yeah.

00:47:14.170 --> 00:47:14.690
She's downstairs.

00:47:15.430 --> 00:47:18.730
And guess why she came calling on Carol and Grant last night?

00:47:19.850 --> 00:47:22.970
It seems that Louise Nelson and Harlow Grant have been wanting to get married.

00:47:23.560 --> 00:47:25.160
But Mrs. Grant wouldn't go for the divorce.

00:47:25.680 --> 00:47:26.860
Except on her terms.

00:47:27.920 --> 00:47:28.520
What terms?

00:47:29.050 --> 00:47:29.970
Half of Grant's...

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:32.760
plus $300,000 cash.

00:47:34.190 --> 00:47:35.110
He couldn't pay it?

00:47:35.430 --> 00:47:36.510
He wouldn't if he could.

00:47:39.740 --> 00:47:40.460
Let's talk to her.

00:47:54.990 --> 00:47:57.860
Nelson, I understand you came here last night

00:47:57.860 --> 00:47:59.600
to ask Mrs. Grant to divorce her husband.

00:48:01.400 --> 00:48:01.900
Oh, yes.

00:48:03.470 --> 00:48:04.370
What time did you leave?

00:48:05.240 --> 00:48:07.060
I don't remember the exact time.

00:48:07.080 --> 00:48:08.020
It was after midnight.

00:48:08.400 --> 00:48:11.090
She put me out almost as soon as I came in.

00:48:11.450 --> 00:48:12.350
Were you angry?

00:48:13.850 --> 00:48:15.570
That woman would make anyone angry, Lieutenant.

00:48:16.230 --> 00:48:18.120
She was greedy and vicious.

00:48:18.980 --> 00:48:23.710
Miss Nelson, do you own any kind of pistol, revolver, automatic?

00:48:25.280 --> 00:48:26.780
No. Why do you ask?

00:48:27.260 --> 00:48:27.880
How about you?

00:48:28.330 --> 00:48:29.150
Do you own any firearms?

00:48:30.730 --> 00:48:31.170
Well, yes.

00:48:31.640 --> 00:48:34.240
Matter of fact, I have a small collection of handguns.

00:48:34.440 --> 00:48:36.860
Early dueling pieces, derringers, things like that.

00:48:37.170 --> 00:48:39.410
Anything modern, cartridge gun?

00:48:40.170 --> 00:48:41.950
Foreign makes, early automatics.

00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:45.520
Mr. Grant, did you come here yourself last night?

00:48:45.940 --> 00:48:46.280
No.

00:48:47.780 --> 00:48:49.760
I was in a place called the King's Tavern,

00:48:50.920 --> 00:48:52.120
getting myself plastered.

00:48:52.980 --> 00:48:53.980
Did a good job of it.

00:48:54.590 --> 00:48:56.610
Meaning that you stayed till closing time.

00:48:57.210 --> 00:48:59.790
And until I woke up in my car in the parking lot.

00:49:00.160 --> 00:49:01.480
About 5 o'clock this morning.

00:49:02.350 --> 00:49:04.870
Well, Mr. Grant, I'll have to ask you to come along with me.

00:49:08.230 --> 00:49:08.830
King's Tavern.

00:49:12.070 --> 00:49:12.670
Be all right, Louise.

00:49:12.910 --> 00:49:24.200
Is this. Thanks a lot, Sandy.

00:49:24.590 --> 00:49:25.810
All right, Mr. Grant. My pleasure.

00:49:28.620 --> 00:49:29.960
Mr. Grant says he left.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:31.080
after you closed up.

00:49:32.140 --> 00:49:34.700
After that, he went out to the parking lot,

00:49:34.960 --> 00:49:37.080
fell asleep in his car till 5 in the morning.

00:49:38.480 --> 00:49:39.080
Verify that?

00:49:39.680 --> 00:49:41.900
Well, I can verify he left here a little after 2.

00:49:42.100 --> 00:49:44.520
As for the parking lot, how would I know?

00:49:45.310 --> 00:49:46.570
I leave right after I lock up.

00:49:47.470 --> 00:49:48.910
How about the parking attendant?

00:49:49.550 --> 00:49:50.970
Oh, he goes home as soon as we close.

00:49:52.730 --> 00:49:54.870
Look, Lieutenant, I was in no condition

00:49:54.870 --> 00:49:56.490
to drive when I left here last night.

00:49:57.000 --> 00:49:58.600
So I went out in the car and slept it off.

00:49:59.700 --> 00:49:59.980
No b----.

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:02.180
But he saw you between the hours of 2 and 5.

00:50:05.060 --> 00:50:07.170
What kind of a mood was he in?

00:50:08.120 --> 00:50:10.840
Happy drunk, sleepy drunk, fighting drunk, what?

00:50:11.040 --> 00:50:15.620
Well, I guess you'd call it a bitter drunk.

00:50:16.800 --> 00:50:20.280
Seems this wife of his, this Carolyn Grant,

00:50:20.990 --> 00:50:22.010
she wouldn't give him a divorce.

00:50:23.800 --> 00:50:24.380
Wait a minute.

00:50:24.540 --> 00:50:27.800
How do you know that?

00:50:28.720 --> 00:50:29.880
Well, you spent half the night, Benny.

00:50:31.110 --> 00:50:36.600
Boy, I must have been drunk. I don't remember.

00:50:36.780 --> 00:50:41.480
Do you by any chance remember driving over to Carol and Grant's studio at 3 a.m.?

00:50:42.460 --> 00:50:45.910
I told you before, I didn't drive anywhere last night.

00:50:46.250 --> 00:50:47.730
Where'd he say he was going after he left?

00:50:48.040 --> 00:50:50.300
He didn't say. All he said was...

00:50:52.310 --> 00:50:52.710
Said what?

00:50:54.880 --> 00:50:56.580
I guess he was kidding.

00:50:56.940 --> 00:50:57.840
Kidding about what?

00:51:00.190 --> 00:51:04.240
about getting rid of his wife with a dull knife.

00:51:05.860 --> 00:51:09.420
Sandy, I might have said it, but I didn't mean it.

00:51:09.640 --> 00:51:10.940
Well, I know that, Mr. Grant.

00:51:11.480 --> 00:51:12.440
What else did he say?

00:51:14.300 --> 00:51:18.750
Well, when I told him that no woman was worth a man

00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:23.240
going to the gas chamber for, he said, I'm not so sure.

00:51:23.420 --> 00:51:24.680
Maybe this one is worth it.

00:51:29.650 --> 00:51:29.970
His wife can't.

00:51:32.170 --> 00:51:36.960
With a gun. Let's get out and take a look at your collection, Mr. Grant.

00:51:37.280 --> 00:51:39.730
I may want to show it to a friend of mine downtown.

00:51:40.330 --> 00:51:41.790
He's quite a collector himself.

00:51:42.640 --> 00:51:48.720
Works for the police department, Bureau of Ballistics.

00:51:55.250 --> 00:51:55.890
Call me again.

00:52:00.380 --> 00:52:01.720
What's the report from ballistics?

00:52:02.310 --> 00:52:04.910
Carolyn Grant was killed with a .25 caliber automatic.

00:52:05.070 --> 00:52:06.470
German make pocket Moser.

00:52:06.590 --> 00:52:07.730
Fires a special cartridge.

00:52:07.930 --> 00:52:08.870
Very few of them in the country.

00:52:09.200 --> 00:52:10.800
Sounds sort of like a collector's item.

00:52:11.740 --> 00:52:13.480
I never owned a gun like that in my life.

00:52:14.770 --> 00:52:15.970
You could be telling the truth.

00:52:16.700 --> 00:52:17.240
How do we know?

00:52:18.660 --> 00:52:20.020
We haven't found the murder weapon yet.

00:52:21.050 --> 00:52:22.410
You still intend to hold me?

00:52:23.060 --> 00:52:24.280
Yes, for further questioning.

00:52:25.210 --> 00:52:25.830
You had a motive.

00:52:26.780 --> 00:52:28.900
You can't prove where you were at the time the crime was...

00:52:31.690 --> 00:52:32.710
Homicide, hostetter.

00:52:35.080 --> 00:52:35.320
Who?

00:52:37.830 --> 00:52:38.570
Say that again.

00:52:42.730 --> 00:52:42.890
Yeah.

00:52:43.920 --> 00:52:45.940
Well, we'll be over at the DA's office in a few minutes, thanks.

00:52:49.450 --> 00:52:50.170
Well, how do you like it?

00:52:51.180 --> 00:52:54.260
Somebody out there in the ante room wants to confess to the Carolyn Grant murder.

00:52:55.200 --> 00:52:55.820
Oh, he's Nelson?

00:52:56.920 --> 00:52:57.200
No.

00:52:58.310 --> 00:52:59.770
Someone we never even thought of.

00:53:00.640 --> 00:53:01.240
His father.

00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:03.260
Why, that's ridiculous.

00:53:03.900 --> 00:53:04.680
He didn't do it.

00:53:05.040 --> 00:53:05.640
How do you know?

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:06.880
He couldn't.

00:53:07.340 --> 00:53:08.400
You're released, Mr. Grant.

00:53:08.770 --> 00:53:11.370
We can't hold you for a crime that somebody else admits to.

00:53:11.550 --> 00:53:12.010
All right, Sergeant.

00:53:12.190 --> 00:53:12.590
Come on, Grant.

00:53:12.820 --> 00:53:13.240
Wait a minute.

00:53:15.130 --> 00:53:16.270
Do you really believe that?

00:53:16.490 --> 00:53:17.390
Goodbye, Mr. Grant.

00:53:28.700 --> 00:53:29.240
Do you believe it?

00:53:32.770 --> 00:53:35.650
Maybe if we give Harlow Grant enough rope, he'll hang himself.

00:53:37.330 --> 00:53:38.410
Let's go to the DA's office.

00:53:38.730 --> 00:53:50.820
Harlow, there must be something we can do to help you, Father.

00:53:51.850 --> 00:53:52.670
Maybe there is.

00:53:53.750 --> 00:53:55.390
Do you think we can get into Carolyn's studio?

00:53:56.660 --> 00:53:59.140
Why not? The place is legally yours now.

00:54:00.090 --> 00:54:01.230
Do you think the police will let us in?

00:54:02.380 --> 00:54:06.060
So? They turned the studio upside down, but they finished about noon.

00:54:06.500 --> 00:54:10.220
I heard the police captain tell somebody it was all right to let the caretaker have his key back.

00:54:10.800 --> 00:54:13.700
Drive there, will you, honey? We'll ask the caretaker to let us in.

00:54:14.420 --> 00:54:14.760
Why?

00:54:15.280 --> 00:54:18.960
For one reason, I want to dispose of Carolyn's personal belongings.

00:54:19.960 --> 00:54:25.010
For another, I think we ought to pack the Ark stuff and get it ready to move.

00:54:26.490 --> 00:54:29.980
Both of those reasons are honest enough. We ought to be good enough for the caretaker.

00:54:30.800 --> 00:54:32.760
What's your real reason for wanting to go there?

00:54:34.400 --> 00:54:35.080
Blind hope.

00:54:35.260 --> 00:54:40.810
I found you another box, Mr. Grant.

00:54:42.410 --> 00:54:44.010
Thanks, Otto. I don't think we'll need it.

00:54:44.360 --> 00:54:47.480
We've packed all the art goods, and I'll put Mrs. Grant's clothing in her luggage.

00:54:47.940 --> 00:54:51.760
Otto, who else had a key to this door? I mean, other than Mrs. Grant.

00:54:52.360 --> 00:54:55.260
Well, me, of course. And then there was Betty Allen.

00:54:55.640 --> 00:54:56.920
She worked for Mrs. Grant.

00:54:57.420 --> 00:54:59.970
She quit her job over the weekend. Didn't she turn in...

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:01.680
To me, she didn't.

00:55:02.660 --> 00:55:04.100
Well, does anybody else have a key?

00:55:04.850 --> 00:55:05.610
Not that I know of.

00:55:06.560 --> 00:55:08.320
Well, what about Mrs. Grant's business partner?

00:55:08.520 --> 00:55:09.260
Didn't he have a key?

00:55:09.440 --> 00:55:10.060
Well, Mr. Vincent?

00:55:10.720 --> 00:55:11.000
No.

00:55:11.460 --> 00:55:11.660
No.

00:55:11.800 --> 00:55:12.960
Mrs. Grant always let him in.

00:55:13.080 --> 00:55:13.800
Oh, Betty Allen.

00:55:13.940 --> 00:55:15.300
He only came around when they were here.

00:55:15.720 --> 00:55:17.280
Where can I find Betty Allen now?

00:55:17.620 --> 00:55:18.440
Where did she live, you mean?

00:55:18.940 --> 00:55:19.460
I don't know.

00:55:20.280 --> 00:55:22.740
She had an apartment on the same street with Mr. Vincent.

00:55:22.920 --> 00:55:24.280
He used to drive her home sometimes,

00:55:24.880 --> 00:55:25.900
before she bought a car.

00:55:26.350 --> 00:55:28.170
Maybe I can get her address from Mr. Vincent.

00:55:28.520 --> 00:55:29.420
Do you know where he lives?

00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:34.000
Yes, the Las Flores' apartments on the corner of the Highland and the Holly Terrace.

00:55:34.570 --> 00:55:36.750
Thanks, Otto. We'll call you if we need anything further.

00:55:37.410 --> 00:55:38.690
Always glad to be of any help.

00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:44.020
You know, my blind hope gets better every minute.

00:55:44.900 --> 00:55:47.180
Honey, run up to Carolyn's room and close the door.

00:55:47.860 --> 00:55:48.500
What for, dear?

00:55:48.560 --> 00:55:49.320
Never mind. Run along.

00:56:13.580 --> 00:56:20.040
If you break a window, if you shatter a pane of glass in the dead of night, it makes a noise.

00:56:20.500 --> 00:56:24.040
Now, even if Carolyn were asleep, that noise would awaken her with a start.

00:56:24.820 --> 00:56:26.860
Now, she had an extension telephone by her bed.

00:56:27.320 --> 00:56:29.440
Why didn't she use that phone to call the police?

00:56:30.440 --> 00:56:30.780
I don't know.

00:56:30.920 --> 00:56:31.480
Why didn't she?

00:56:31.850 --> 00:56:34.790
Because when that window was broken, she was already dead.

00:56:35.340 --> 00:56:36.640
And the person who broke that window

00:56:36.640 --> 00:56:38.920
wanted the police to believe that that was the way they got in.

00:56:39.480 --> 00:56:40.800
Actually, she got in with a key.

00:56:42.380 --> 00:56:42.700
She?

00:56:43.260 --> 00:56:44.500
Betty Allen had a key.

00:56:46.280 --> 00:56:47.140
What was her motive?

00:56:47.360 --> 00:56:49.440
She said she and Carolyn parted the best of friends.

00:56:50.320 --> 00:56:51.400
She might have been lying.

00:56:52.300 --> 00:56:53.400
She also had an alibi.

00:56:53.520 --> 00:56:55.300
She was with her boyfriend at the time of the murder.

00:56:55.840 --> 00:56:57.180
She might have been lying about that, too.

00:56:58.490 --> 00:56:59.970
She said her boyfriend lived on his ..

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:00.820
boat in Newport.

00:57:01.880 --> 00:57:03.980
No sense in wasting a drive if neither of them

00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:04.540
happened to be there.

00:57:08.260 --> 00:57:09.540
Operator, I'd like some information

00:57:09.540 --> 00:57:10.840
on her number in Newport.

00:57:13.570 --> 00:57:14.430
Bailey's Boat Yard.

00:57:15.670 --> 00:57:16.430
Dick Sawyer.

00:57:17.480 --> 00:57:19.520
No, his station wagon's not here.

00:57:20.820 --> 00:57:22.260
I think he had to drive to town.

00:57:22.570 --> 00:57:24.930
Do you happen to know if a Miss Betty Allen is with him?

00:57:25.240 --> 00:57:25.640
Betty?

00:57:25.860 --> 00:57:26.420
Oh, no.

00:57:26.680 --> 00:57:28.300
She wouldn't be with Dick, not anymore.

00:57:28.760 --> 00:57:29.640
They broke up.

00:57:30.570 --> 00:57:32.230
They want? When did that happen?

00:57:36.310 --> 00:57:38.580
Carolyn and Betty Allen did have a fight, and guess why?

00:57:43.220 --> 00:57:44.360
No, no thank you, no message.

00:57:46.080 --> 00:57:48.540
Carolyn busted up Betty Allen's engagement to Dick Sawyer.

00:57:49.760 --> 00:57:52.640
This Allen girl told the police that she and Carolyn got along fine.

00:57:52.800 --> 00:57:53.400
No, she lied.

00:57:55.480 --> 00:57:58.120
I wonder who she's covering up for, herself or her boyfriend?

00:57:59.620 --> 00:57:59.980
I'll ask...

00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:01.140
It's Gwaine Vincent, where she lives.

00:58:01.320 --> 00:58:02.000
I'll go with you.

00:58:02.160 --> 00:58:02.660
No, no, honey.

00:58:03.360 --> 00:58:05.960
If Betty Allen does have a 25 automatic in her hand,

00:58:06.180 --> 00:58:07.140
I don't want you with me.

00:58:08.200 --> 00:58:09.120
I'll borrow your car.

00:58:09.460 --> 00:58:11.160
You run upstairs and finish that packing.

00:58:11.340 --> 00:58:12.360
I wish you wouldn't go alone.

00:58:12.500 --> 00:58:13.280
Can't you call the police?

00:58:13.640 --> 00:58:16.260
No, I've got a hunch I'll do better if I just walk in on her.

00:58:31.950 --> 00:58:39.290
Grant, I was wondering how I might contact you.

00:58:39.520 --> 00:58:41.660
Oh, what did you want to contact me about?

00:58:41.840 --> 00:58:44.260
Well, as you know, I was Mrs. Grant's business partner,

00:58:44.460 --> 00:58:46.430
and a few of the little paintings over at the studio

00:58:46.430 --> 00:58:49.370
happened to be my own personal property, and I'd like to get them back.

00:58:50.300 --> 00:58:53.710
You can stop by my home. I'll give you a card with my address.

00:58:54.770 --> 00:58:58.030
I've had all of Carolyn's art objects wrapped and stacked for the movers.

00:58:58.470 --> 00:58:59.970
They're going to pick them up the first thing in the morning.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:03.490
Transfer them to my home. Here's the address.

00:59:03.670 --> 00:59:04.950
You can pick them up any time after 10.

00:59:05.250 --> 00:59:07.930
Now, I, uh, I'd like to ask you for an address.

00:59:08.650 --> 00:59:10.810
The, uh, caretaker at the art studio,

00:59:10.810 --> 00:59:12.570
so that you might help me find Betty Allen.

00:59:13.510 --> 00:59:15.750
Oh, yes, she's at the Fairview Court.

00:59:15.970 --> 00:59:21.870
Uh, I, uh, naturally, I always think a man's innocent until proven guilty,

00:59:21.970 --> 00:59:26.860
but the last newsflash I heard on my radio said that you were still being held as a suspect.

00:59:27.600 --> 00:59:29.420
Yes, uh, I've been released.

00:59:30.280 --> 00:59:31.160
They're now holding my father.

00:59:32.560 --> 00:59:34.480
You mean for what happened to Carolyn?

00:59:35.920 --> 00:59:37.060
Oh, surely they don't think.

00:59:37.140 --> 00:59:38.040
They may think he's guilty.

00:59:38.220 --> 00:59:38.800
I don't.

00:59:39.370 --> 00:59:41.010
He only confessed because he thought

00:59:41.010 --> 00:59:42.130
he might get me off the hook.

00:59:42.390 --> 00:59:43.530
Your father confessed?

00:59:43.790 --> 00:59:45.090
His confession won't mean a thing

00:59:45.090 --> 00:59:46.750
when they start asking him to back it up.

00:59:47.340 --> 00:59:49.600
You see, in the first place, my father's never shot a gun.

00:59:49.840 --> 00:59:52.220
He doesn't even know the make or caliber of the murder weapon.

00:59:53.080 --> 00:59:53.920
But the police know?

00:59:54.060 --> 00:59:56.320
Well, from the ballistics report, they'll

00:59:56.320 --> 00:59:58.840
ask him where he got the gun, what the caliber was,

00:59:59.350 --> 00:59:59.970
what he did with it.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:01.060
after he shot Carolyn.

01:00:01.850 --> 01:00:03.450
Dad doesn't know enough about guns

01:00:03.450 --> 01:00:05.430
to make his confession stick for even a day.

01:00:06.460 --> 01:00:08.700
You say that Betty Allen is at the Fairview?

01:00:09.180 --> 01:00:11.900
Mm-hmm. It's across the street, apartment 2C.

01:00:12.220 --> 01:00:14.600
Do you mind if I ask why you're going to see Betty Allen?

01:00:16.220 --> 01:00:18.830
You may ask. I don't have time to answer.

01:00:41.520 --> 01:00:42.820
May I please see you for a moment, Ms. Allen?

01:00:43.660 --> 01:00:46.130
Well, I was expecting somebody.

01:00:47.700 --> 01:00:48.120
All right.

01:00:49.040 --> 01:00:52.570
I see you haven't gotten your engagement ring back

01:00:52.570 --> 01:00:53.390
from the jewelers yet.

01:00:54.170 --> 01:00:56.150
That is the story you told the police, isn't it?

01:00:57.220 --> 01:00:59.020
Just what are you trying to imply?

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.560
Your ring never went to the jewelers at all.

01:01:02.170 --> 01:01:05.270
That you put it in an envelope, gave it to the girl at Bailey's boatyard,

01:01:05.740 --> 01:01:09.420
asked you to give it to Dick Sawyer when he returned from his little fishing trip with Carolyn.

01:01:10.450 --> 01:01:13.030
Are there any other lies you care to accuse me of, Mr. Grant?

01:01:14.140 --> 01:01:14.720
Lots more.

01:01:15.240 --> 01:01:17.800
You said that you had no quarrel with Carolyn.

01:01:18.270 --> 01:01:19.730
That was the biggest lie of all.

01:01:20.140 --> 01:01:22.360
You quarreled with her over this fellow Dick Sawyer.

01:01:23.310 --> 01:01:24.730
She broke up your engagement with him.

01:01:25.620 --> 01:01:27.240
That's why you quit your job.

01:01:28.060 --> 01:01:29.480
That's why you killed Carolyn.

01:01:31.210 --> 01:01:31.810
I what?

01:01:32.610 --> 01:01:34.470
You've been caught in your own lies, and you know it.

01:01:34.680 --> 01:01:36.320
It's about time you started telling the truth.

01:01:36.540 --> 01:01:37.820
You did kill Carolyn, didn't you?

01:01:37.920 --> 01:01:39.620
Hey, take your hands off her.

01:01:44.230 --> 01:01:44.630
Dick.

01:01:45.290 --> 01:01:46.330
So you're both in on the murder.

01:01:46.920 --> 01:01:48.320
Hey, honey, who is this joker?

01:01:48.380 --> 01:01:49.140
What's he talking about?

01:01:50.210 --> 01:01:50.930
Harlow Grant.

01:01:51.090 --> 01:01:51.930
He's her husband.

01:01:52.290 --> 01:01:54.680
He somehow found out I lied to the police.

01:01:55.290 --> 01:01:57.310
Well, then why not start telling the truth?

01:01:57.800 --> 01:01:59.040
Well, that's what I advised her.

01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:01.600
I was afraid to admit I lied.

01:02:01.900 --> 01:02:03.400
Will they prosecute me for it?

01:02:04.090 --> 01:02:06.680
Well, I don't know, honey, but being prosecuted for lying

01:02:06.680 --> 01:02:08.620
isn't nearly as bad as being prosecuted for murder.

01:02:09.130 --> 01:02:10.670
Then she admits that she was lying.

01:02:11.150 --> 01:02:12.490
But not for herself, for me.

01:02:12.550 --> 01:02:13.630
She thought I killed Karen.

01:02:14.260 --> 01:02:17.470
Oh, not really, Dick, but I did know you left here

01:02:17.470 --> 01:02:18.650
mad enough to do something.

01:02:18.850 --> 01:02:20.360
I tried to stop you.

01:02:20.460 --> 01:02:21.900
I talked to her on the phone from Newport

01:02:21.900 --> 01:02:22.700
a couple hours ago.

01:02:22.860 --> 01:02:24.180
We got the whole mess straightened out.

01:02:24.510 --> 01:02:27.400
And I can prove that I was back in Newport before 3 AM.

01:02:28.650 --> 01:02:29.970
Then if neither of you

01:02:30.220 --> 01:02:31.000
Killed Carolyn.

01:02:31.360 --> 01:02:31.900
Who did?

01:02:32.800 --> 01:02:33.460
How do we know?

01:02:34.380 --> 01:02:37.180
You by chance know if any of Carolyn's friends or enemies

01:02:37.180 --> 01:02:38.980
owned a 25 automatic.

01:02:40.100 --> 01:02:43.620
Do you mean one of those little German guns, a Mauser?

01:02:46.080 --> 01:02:47.900
What makes you think I meant a Mauser?

01:02:49.410 --> 01:02:51.410
I guess because the only automatic pistol

01:02:51.410 --> 01:02:53.290
I ever saw happened to be a Mauser.

01:02:53.530 --> 01:02:55.610
Wayne Vincent gave one to Carolyn for a present.

01:02:56.520 --> 01:02:58.660
Then Carolyn could have been killed with her own gun.

01:02:59.160 --> 01:02:59.980
Did she give her a gun?

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:00.580
Give it to anyone?

01:03:00.740 --> 01:03:01.080
Loan it?

01:03:01.590 --> 01:03:02.470
I don't think so.

01:03:02.650 --> 01:03:05.130
It was still there yesterday when I cleaned up the desk.

01:03:05.520 --> 01:03:06.940
She kept it in the desk?

01:03:07.470 --> 01:03:08.550
In the top middle drawer.

01:03:10.070 --> 01:03:13.070
Did you tell the police that Carolyn owned a 25 automatic?

01:03:14.310 --> 01:03:16.070
They didn't ask me if Carolyn owned a gun.

01:03:16.150 --> 01:03:18.350
They only asked if I owned one, and I don't.

01:03:19.530 --> 01:03:21.730
And if Carolyn were killed with her own gun,

01:03:22.330 --> 01:03:25.050
whoever killed her knew where that gun was kept.

01:03:25.210 --> 01:03:26.370
Now, don't start accusing Betty.

01:03:26.470 --> 01:03:28.030
Other people might have known where that gun was kept.

01:03:28.260 --> 01:03:29.100
That's quite possible.

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:31.940
The police will be interested in two facts.

01:03:32.690 --> 01:03:34.130
Betty knew where the gun was.

01:03:34.570 --> 01:03:35.990
She has a key to the studio.

01:03:36.660 --> 01:03:37.920
I don't have a key.

01:03:38.120 --> 01:03:40.340
I did have, but I left it there when I quit.

01:03:41.260 --> 01:03:42.740
You left it with the caretaker?

01:03:43.190 --> 01:03:45.330
No, I left it with Wayne Vincent.

01:03:45.630 --> 01:03:47.310
He stayed at the studio yesterday

01:03:47.310 --> 01:03:50.160
while Carolyn was supposed to be in Laguna.

01:03:50.980 --> 01:03:53.040
Then Wayne Vincent had a key last night.

01:03:53.180 --> 01:03:54.060
He had your key.

01:03:55.200 --> 01:03:59.530
I guess so, unless he gave it to Carolyn or to the caretaker.

01:04:00.800 --> 01:04:03.360
Did Vincent know where Carolyn kept the gun?

01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:07.360
I suppose so. He used the desk quite often.

01:04:09.040 --> 01:04:13.060
Wayne Vincent had a key. He also had access to the gun.

01:04:14.550 --> 01:04:17.190
Can you think of any reason why he might want to kill Carolyn?

01:04:19.480 --> 01:04:23.620
Not unless she messed up his life, like she almost messed up ours.

01:04:25.540 --> 01:04:27.630
Thanks for everything. Thanks a lot.

01:04:35.340 --> 01:04:40.760
Good night, Miss Sika.

01:04:40.940 --> 01:04:42.220
Good night, Otto. See you tomorrow.

01:05:56.170 --> 01:05:59.720
There was anyone here you scared me you scared me

01:06:02.040 --> 01:06:03.060
I thought I'd lock the door.

01:06:03.450 --> 01:06:04.390
Oh, you did lock it.

01:06:04.800 --> 01:06:07.280
But as Mrs. Grant's business partner, I have a key, too.

01:06:08.210 --> 01:06:10.130
A few of these artworks happen to be my own,

01:06:10.190 --> 01:06:11.530
and I just dropped by to pick them up.

01:06:11.630 --> 01:06:13.250
I'm not stealing anything, I assure you.

01:06:15.120 --> 01:06:16.060
Am I stealing these?

01:06:16.990 --> 01:06:19.250
Mr. Grant asked me to gather up his wife's things.

01:06:20.550 --> 01:06:22.350
I hope I didn't disturb you.

01:06:23.320 --> 01:06:24.860
I'll just take a few minutes, and then I'll go.

01:06:25.350 --> 01:06:26.730
You're not disturbing me, in the least.

01:06:27.920 --> 01:06:29.980
If you don't mind, I'll...

01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:33.910
I'll go on with my job. Mr. Grant's calling for me in just a few minutes.

01:06:56.260 --> 01:06:59.210
Would you get me the police department, please? This might be an emergency.

01:07:03.160 --> 01:07:06.470
Hello, would you connect me with either Captain Halstead or Lieutenant Colton?

01:07:06.730 --> 01:07:13.000
Right away, please. It's homicide.

01:07:15.140 --> 01:07:19.840
Hello? Hello? Hello, operator?

01:07:30.760 --> 01:07:40.220
A minute when I sit, Mr. Grant will be here any minute.

01:07:40.520 --> 01:07:41.540
My car's outside.

01:07:42.020 --> 01:07:44.340
If we should meet him, remember this will be in my pocket.

01:07:44.930 --> 01:07:46.150
Tell him to get into the car with us.

01:07:46.230 --> 01:07:46.690
He can drive.

01:07:47.180 --> 01:07:48.400
We don't meet him, you can drive.

01:07:48.780 --> 01:07:49.020
Where?

01:07:49.700 --> 01:07:50.920
I'll decide the destination.

01:07:52.300 --> 01:07:56.750
Tell him you'll be right down.

01:08:02.110 --> 01:08:03.990
Oh, shit.

01:08:33.960 --> 01:08:35.700
I'll kill her if you make one move.

01:08:37.610 --> 01:08:39.350
She's standing right where Carolyn stood.

01:08:39.890 --> 01:08:41.950
Do you want to see her fall down the steps like she did?

01:08:42.090 --> 01:08:50.370
All right, Vincent.

01:08:56.260 --> 01:08:58.060
Look what Santa Claus brought us.

01:08:58.300 --> 01:08:58.960
Exhibit A.

01:09:00.000 --> 01:09:02.740
He took that gun out of his pocket and hid it in one of the packing cases.

01:09:03.040 --> 01:09:04.830
I was on the balcony. He didn't see me.

01:09:04.990 --> 01:09:09.670
He put the gun in one of the boxes because I was dumb enough to tell him that the boxes were being delivered to my house.

01:09:10.000 --> 01:09:10.300
Why?

01:09:10.750 --> 01:09:13.130
Because he knew that the Grant family was already in hot water.

01:09:13.560 --> 01:09:15.660
And planting the gun on the Grants would drown.

01:09:16.760 --> 01:09:19.750
You fellas sure got here at the right time. A guardian angel must have sent you.

01:09:20.160 --> 01:09:22.620
Your guardian angel goes under the name of Captain Hostetter.

01:09:22.800 --> 01:09:24.580
He's had us tailing you ever since you were released.

01:09:25.250 --> 01:09:26.390
You follow us now to headquarters.

01:09:27.240 --> 01:09:28.000
Yeah, I'll be with you in a minute.
